WEBVTT

00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:03.287
Once a script made that list,
it made the blacklist.

00:01:03.287 --> 00:01:05.996
And then powerful people started to
see that there was consensus that

00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:07.371
the script was actually amazing.

00:01:07.788 --> 00:01:10.788
Well, then, these previously
unsellable projects,

00:01:10.996 --> 00:01:13.913
they started getting sold and getting
made and winning awards.

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:15.788
And here's how Franklin describes

00:01:15.788 --> 00:01:18.663
the importance of that in his
talk at Ted Venice Beach.

00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:24.038
Simply put, the conventional wisdom about
screenwriting merit where it was

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:27.204
and where it could be found was wrong.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.121
And this is notable because,
as I mentioned before,